<meta title="Counting Elephants (child fallback)" />

Aerial transects and ground counts are the two standard survey methods for
savanna elephants.

## Aerial Transects

Aerial transects remain the standard method. See <ref @fig:transect> for the grid
layout; in a book it resolves to a chapter-scoped number (figure 1.1, not figure 1).

<fig #fig:transect src=transect.png | A standard aerial-transect grid.>

## Ground Counts

Ground counts complement the aerial survey at known aggregation points such as
waterholes during the dry season.
